ions of  dollars and elon is tweeting about dog  money there's a ton of noise in the  crypto space as well as plenty of scams  so be careful out there and quickly i'll  never ask you to message a random phone  number in the comments but you can  subscribe to the channel now once we  separate out all the junk and get to the  core of the technology we need to ask  how can crypto actually help build the  metaverse well the first area is  interoperability right now that  basically just means bringing a digital  asset from one game into another which  might seem silly but remember the  virtual economy already generates over  50 billion dollars per year and that's  without any crypto but honestly who  cares if you can bring a minecraft skin  into call of duty does that really  create any meaningful value or advanced  technology even the slightest bit as  silly as all this sounds i actually do  think it's an important step forward  here's why right now every traditional  tech company is building its own little  walled garden epic games makes fortnite  you buy a skin in fortnite it lives in  fortnite forever now epic games could  allow digital assets from other games to  transfer into fortnite they might need  to build a complex pipeline to transfer  the assets over or define an open  standard but they could do it the only  reason that they don't is because it  would hurt their business epic wants to  be the only company that can sell  dancing bananas in fortnite but if  crypto can break down these wild gardens  the playing field will get a lot more  competitive creators building any small  piece of the metaverse will be able to  ensure that what they build continues to  make them money forever if you can  accept the fact that the 50 billion  virtual economy is basically real at  this point it becomes a lot clearer why  crypto might prove useful here a virtual  asset might be bought in one game and  then sold in another making sure the  creator gets a small royalty payment 